    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `label_ticket` in `app/labeler.py`, and `pytest -q` passes (1 test). That test only checks that `LABELS` are lowercase, so nothing tests `label_ticket` itself. I also haven't called the real API.\n\nWhat it does:\n- Sends one `client.messages.create` request to `MODEL` (`claude-sonnet-4-6`) with `max_tokens=5` and `temperature=0`.\n- The system prompt is \"Classify the support ticket. Answer with exactly one word from: bug, feature, question.\" It's built from `LABELS`, so it stays in sync if the labels change.\n- The ticket text is sent as the user message.\n- It joins the text blocks of the reply, strips and lower-cases the result, and returns it if it's in `LABELS`. Anything else returns `\"question\"`.\n\n**Temperature 0 only works while `MODEL` stays on Sonnet 4.6.** Newer models (Sonnet 5, Opus 4.7 and later, Fable) return a 400 error if the request includes `temperature`. `app/summaries.py` also uses `MODEL`, so upgrading it later would break the labeler.\n\nOne small point on the fallback: a reply like \"Bug.\" still has its full stop after stripping, so it doesn't match a label and returns `\"question\"`. That's what you specified, but I can remove trailing punctuation too if you'd like.\n\nNo dependencies were added."
